      "topic": "Energy",
      "prompt": "As countries search for alternatives to fossil fuels, some governments are investing heavily in nuclear power to meet their energy needs. Do the advantages of nuclear energy outweigh the disadvantages?",
      "modelAnswer": "With the world urgently seeking alternatives to polluting fossil fuels, nuclear power has returned to the centre of energy debates, and several governments are expanding their reactor programmes. While nuclear energy involves undeniable dangers, I believe that on balance its advantages outweigh its disadvantages.\n\nThe chief benefit of nuclear power is its ability to generate vast amounts of electricity with minimal carbon emissions. Unlike coal or gas, a nuclear plant produces almost no greenhouse gases during operation, making it a powerful tool against climate change. France, for instance, derives the majority of its electricity from nuclear reactors and consequently enjoys some of the lowest carbon emissions in the industrialised world. Nuclear energy is also highly reliable, supplying constant power regardless of weather, unlike solar or wind, which makes it ideal for meeting steady national demand.\n\nHowever, the disadvantages are serious and cannot be dismissed. The most alarming is the risk of catastrophic accidents, as demonstrated by the disasters at Chernobyl and Fukushima, which rendered large areas uninhabitable for decades. In addition, nuclear plants produce radioactive waste that remains hazardous for thousands of years, and humanity has yet to devise a fully secure long-term storage solution. The enormous cost and lengthy construction time of new reactors present further obstacles.\n\nDespite these grave concerns, I would argue that modern reactor designs are far safer than earlier models, and serious accidents remain extremely rare relative to the deaths caused annually by fossil-fuel pollution. Given the existential threat of climate change, nuclear power offers an indispensable low-carbon option.\n\nIn conclusion, although nuclear energy carries risks of accidents and waste, its capacity to deliver reliable, clean electricity at scale means its advantages outweigh its disadvantages."
